  "status": "SUCCESS",
  "summary": "Explored the flashcard CLI codebase (4 source files, 1 test file) and documented findings. The app has a simple architecture: Card data type with id/front/back/tags/createdAt fields, a QuizSession that iterates cards linearly with boolean correct/incorrect answers, and a ScoreSummary scorer. There is no persistence (loadCards is a stub), no card selection logic, and no review tracking. SM-2 integration requires: (1) a new ReviewState type with repetition/easeFactor/interval/nextReviewDate fields, (2) expanding boolean answers to a quality grade scale (0-5), (3) due-card selection logic, and (4) file-based persistence. Recommended approach is a separate sm2.ts module with pure functions, keeping the Card interface unchanged, using a 3-tier grade UX (Again/Good/Easy), and separate JSON files for cards vs review state.",
