dAt, YYYY-MM-DD for SM-2 dates) is reasonable but deserves a brief rationale note.\n\nThe SM-2 algorithm implementation spec in sm2-engine.md is accurate. The formula for EF update matches the original Wozniak SM-2 paper. The interval progression (1, 6, then EF-scaled) is correct. The test cases enumerated are comprehensive and cover edge cases (EF floor, reset on failure, date arithmetic).\n\nThe storage design is appropriate for the scale of a personal CLI flashcard tool. Atomic writes and in-memory migration are sensible choices. The error handling strategy (empty array for missing file, throw for corrupt JSON) is reasonable.\n\nRecommendation: Address the IMPORTANT issues (ReviewRecord completeness, Map serialization awareness) before implementation. The MINOR issues can be deferred or documented as known limitations."
}
```

